       the build-time-downloaded mpdecimal source). CONFIG_32 / PPRO
       must match the flavour LibMpdec was built with so mpdecimal.h
       picks the 32-bit typedef + x87 inline-asm code paths in this
       module's source — same as CPython's bundled
       _decimal.vcxproj on Win32.

       BUILD_LIBMPDEC is needed because mpdecimal32vc.h decorates every
       mpd_* prototype with __declspec(dllimport) when _DLL is defined
       (which MSVC sets automatically under /MD) and BUILD_LIBMPDEC is
       not. Without this define, _decimal.obj emits __imp__mpd_* IAT
       references that the static libmpdec.lib (no import library) can't
       satisfy, and the link fails with "unresolved external symbol
       __imp__mpd_sign" et al. CPython's own _decimal.vcxproj sets
       BUILD_LIBMPDEC for the same reason. -->
